       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily for adults, and 50 mg is five times that. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because of amlodipine's long half-life, that effect could last for days.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Standard dosing:** I can enter 5 mg by mouth once daily. That is the usual starting dose, and it can be titrated up to 10 mg.\n- **Maximum dose:** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily if you want the highest labeled dose.\n- **Dose typo:** If you meant 5 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n- **Blood pressure not controlled on 10 mg:** The usual next step is to add another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. I can enter that order if you tell me the drug and dose.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
